&lt;li&gt;A genuine interest in programming languages, IDEs, and developer tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative mindset, working closely with engineering peers to solve technical puzzles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A balanced approach to testing, valuing both deep exploratory manual testing and systematic automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A habit of raising the bar, leaving codebases and systems cleaner than you found them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll need&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to read and write clean code to create test examples, investigate failures, and build automated tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Kotlin, Java, or another object-oriented programming language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing test scenarios and deciding what should be automated versus tested manually.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with bug trackers, version control, and continuous integration systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Java technologies, frameworks, and build tools like Maven or Gradle.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to analyze complex technical behaviors, such as static analysis, compilers, or language tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
